    Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;27;-352,-736;Inherit;False;525.7374;211.1802;New
    Note;;0,0,0,1;The Vertex Position node outputs the vertices position in object
    space. $$This data is extracted directly from the mesh and contains the vertex
    position relative to the object origin, this means the position values don't
    change whatever transform value your gameobject has. $$This is usually useful
    to use in the Local Vertex Offset output or to create effects that are bound
    to the object and stay exactly the same even if your gameobject changes position,
    rotation or size.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode, AmplifyShaderEditor,
    Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;35;-256,80;Inherit;False;218.9306;112.6857;XYZ;;0,0,0,1;Scales
    away from center of object;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode, AmplifyShaderEditor,
    Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;36;-352,-512;Inherit;False;511.436;161.8565;;;0,0,0,1;XYZW:
    Retrieves the 3 coordinates position and one more. $$This is mostly useful to
    facilitate matrix transformation operations where the W value is needed with
    the value 1 or if you want to retrieve packed data in the W channel.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;38;912,80;Inherit;False;218.9306;112.6857;XYZ;;0,0,0,1;Scales
    in direction of normal;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode, AmplifyShaderEditor,
    Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;45;176,576;Inherit;False;218.9306;112.6857;XYZ;;0,0,0,1;Scales
    based on texture Displacment Sample;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;57;1296,576;Inherit;False;208.7252;119.7766;;;0,0,0,1;The
    Power node adjusts the contrast of the effect.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;58;1040,576;Inherit;False;217.201;130.4018;;;0,0,0,1;Your
    adjustments by vary depending on the height of the character and location of
    the character's pivot point.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode, AmplifyShaderEditor,
    Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;59;784,576;Inherit;False;239.8028;158.6543;;;0,0,0,1;Here's
    we're adjusting the length and position of the gradient so that it matches our
    sphere.  The multiply shrinks the gradient's range, and the add move the dark
    end of the gradient down to the bottom of the character.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;60;512,528;Inherit;False;239.8028;141.7028;;;0,0,0,1;In
    stylized character art, some artists like to apply a gradient to their charactger
    to the the area at the feet of the character is darker, and the character gets
    brighter toward the head.  ;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.PosVertexDataNode,
